From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150: fix the SLPI FastRPC node

The sensor PD on the SLPI reads its registry back from the application
processor through a FastRPC reverse tunnel, and on hotdogb every attach
(INIT_ATTACH and INIT_ATTACH_SNS alike) kills the DSP:

  arm-smmu 15000000.iommu: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x402,
                           iova=0x1fffff000, cbfrsynra=0x5a1
  qcom_q6v5_pas 2400000.remoteproc: fatal error received:
                           EX:sensor_process:0x1:frpck_0_0:0x5b

The only upstream SLPI with a working sensor stack is sdm845, and its
fastrpc node has a shape this one does not: one compute context bank with
no iommus at all, a qcom,vmids list, and a 16 MiB shared-dma-pool the
driver hands to the DSP through a hypervisor call.  The sensor process is
hypervisor-bypassed on the SMMU and works with physical addresses, which is
why the pool alone is not enough.

sm8150 instead attaches three translated context banks (0x5a1-0x5a3) to the
same stream IDs, so the DSP's first access lands in a page table it was
never meant to see and faults.  Mirror sdm845: publish a single
compute-cb@0 without iommus, list the VMIDs the pool has to be assigned to,
and give the node the pool itself.  The pool is 16 MiB, 4 MiB aligned and
reusable, matching downstream's adsp_region.

Without the pool the driver has nothing to hand over; without qcom,vmids
qcom_scm_assign_mem() has no destination and fails with -EINVAL, which is
fatal for the sdsp domain.

Signed-off-by: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi | 29 +++++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
@@ -688,6 +688,14 @@
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
 
+		fastrpc_mem: fastrpc-mem {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0xffffffff>;
+			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
+			size = <0x0 0x1000000>;
+			reusable;
+		};
+
 		hyp_mem: memory@85700000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x85700000 0x0 0x600000>;
 			no-map;
@@ -2220,26 +2228,15 @@
 					qcom,glink-channels = "fastrpcglink-apps-dsp";
 					label = "sdsp";
 					qcom,non-secure-domain;
+					qcom,vmids = <QCOM_SCM_VMID_HLOS QCOM_SCM_VMID_MSS_MSA
+						      QCOM_SCM_VMID_SSC_Q6 QCOM_SCM_VMID_ADSP_Q6>;
+					memory-region = <&fastrpc_mem>;
 					#address-cells = <1>;
 					#size-cells = <0>;
 
-					compute-cb@1 {
-						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
-						reg = <1>;
-						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x05a1 0x0>;
-					};
-
-					compute-cb@2 {
-						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
-						reg = <2>;
-						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x05a2 0x0>;
-					};
-
-					compute-cb@3 {
+					compute-cb@0 {
 						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
-						reg = <3>;
-						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x05a3 0x0>;
-						/* note: shared-cb = <4> in downstream */
+						reg = <0>;
 					};
 				};
 			};
